RDKEMW-20680: Provide a vault_processor_release() no-op for the OpenSSL
and Thunder vault backends.

Follow-up to RDKEMW-19048.  That change added vault_processor_release()
only to the SecApi backend, because that is the one that holds an SA2
SecProcessor handle across deep sleep.  But the shared CryptographyExtAccess
plugin (entservices-cryptography) declares and calls the symbol
unconditionally from onPowerModeChanged, regardless of which vault
implementation the platform compiles.  The cryptography library links
exactly one backend (CRYPTOGRAPHY_IMPLEMENTATION), so platforms that build
OpenSSL (RDKM community: BCM/RTK/RPI) or the Thunder RPC vault fail to load
the plugin:

    symbol lookup error: libWPEFrameworkCryptographyExtAccess.so:
    undefined symbol: vault_processor_release

Neither the OpenSSL nor the Thunder backend holds a SecAPI SecProcessor
handle across S3, so there is nothing to release - a no-op satisfies the
ABI and lets the plugin load and deep sleep proceed.  The SecApi backend
keeps its real handle-releasing implementation (0002-RDKEMW-19048-...patch).

Reported-by: Ligin Abraham Punoose <Ligin_Punoose@comcast.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Sergiy Gladkyy <sgladkyy@productengine.com>

Index: git/Source/cryptography/implementation/OpenSSL/Vault.cpp
===================================================================
--- git.orig/Source/cryptography/implementation/OpenSSL/Vault.cpp
+++ git/Source/cryptography/implementation/OpenSSL/Vault.cpp
@@ -532,5 +532,13 @@ uint32_t persistent_flush(struct VaultImplementation* /* vault */)
 {
     return (WPEFramework::Core::ERROR_UNAVAILABLE);
 }
+
+void vault_processor_release(void)
+{
+    // OpenSSL vault holds no SecAPI SecProcessor handle across deep sleep;
+    // nothing to release. Provide the symbol so the shared
+    // CryptographyExtAccess plugin links on OpenSSL-vault platforms.
+    // See SecApi/Vault.cpp for the handle-releasing implementation.
+}

 } // extern "C"
Index: git/Source/cryptography/implementation/Thunder/Vault.cpp
===================================================================
--- git.orig/Source/cryptography/implementation/Thunder/Vault.cpp
+++ git/Source/cryptography/implementation/Thunder/Vault.cpp
@@ -258,5 +258,13 @@ uint32_t persistent_flush(struct VaultImplementation* vault)
 {
     return(WPEFramework::Core::ERROR_UNAVAILABLE);
 }
+
+void vault_processor_release(void)
+{
+    // Thunder (RPC) vault holds no SecAPI SecProcessor handle across deep
+    // sleep; nothing to release. Provide the symbol so the shared
+    // CryptographyExtAccess plugin links on Thunder-vault platforms.
+    // See SecApi/Vault.cpp for the handle-releasing implementation.
+}

 } // extern "C"
